WEBVTT

00:02.800 --> 00:05.712
So I'm thinking we serve the good wine
before the ceremony...

00:05.880 --> 00:08.758
...and then at the reception,
after everybody's got a buzz on...

00:08.920 --> 00:10.911
...we uncork the crap.

00:11.760 --> 00:16.311
Alan, I do not want to cheap out on
what is very possibly my last wedding.

00:18.040 --> 00:19.155
He's always been stingy.

00:19.320 --> 00:22.756
I remember once when he was a little
boy, he accidentally swallowed a quarter.

00:22.920 --> 00:25.229
Refused to poop for a week.

00:26.200 --> 00:28.919
Mom, for God's sakes,
this is my future stepsister.

00:29.080 --> 00:31.310
Oh, relax, Alan. I think it's cute.

00:31.480 --> 00:35.473
Cute? He's so tight, I wouldn't have been
surprised if only two dimes came out.

00:37.680 --> 00:39.636
Mom, I'm begging you.

00:40.400 --> 00:43.392
Would you feel better if I told you
something embarrassing about me?

00:43.560 --> 00:45.232
- Yes.
- Promise not to laugh?

00:45.840 --> 00:48.035
- I promise.
- All right.

00:48.240 --> 00:51.994
I have never in my life refused to poop.

00:57.480 --> 01:00.597
You are so mean. I love you.

01:01.440 --> 01:03.908
I think I liked it better
when you two didn't get along.

01:04.080 --> 01:05.399
Well, those days are over.

01:05.560 --> 01:09.075
Once I saw how happy Evy makes
my father, I could've married her myself.

01:09.240 --> 01:12.755
Oh, thank you, sweetheart.
And you're like the daughter I never had.

01:12.920 --> 01:14.114
Not that he didn't try.

01:17.720 --> 01:21.190
You should have seen him parading
around in my earrings and my high heels.

01:21.360 --> 01:23.316
"Look at me, Mommy, I'm pretty."

01:25.880 --> 01:26.995
He wasn't, of course.

01:29.880 --> 01:32.553
Oh, darling, I'm just teasing you.

01:32.720 --> 01:33.869
You're all man.

01:35.160 --> 01:36.559
Thanks.

01:36.720 --> 01:38.119
Okay, let's talk appetizers.

01:38.800 --> 01:43.112
Hey, Alan, how long do I have
before Bridezilla gets here?

01:43.520 --> 01:46.990
Gee, Charlie,
I don't know what you're talking about.

01:47.160 --> 01:49.116
She's already here, isn't she?

01:49.280 --> 01:51.032
Yes, dear. Come on down.

01:52.000 --> 01:53.228
It's a little game we play.

01:53.400 --> 01:56.472
I show him unconditional love,
and he's an ungrateful little pissant.

01:59.520 --> 02:01.078
- Hey, Mom.
- Hello, dear.

02:01.240 --> 02:03.151
You remember Teddy's daughter,
Courtney?

02:03.320 --> 02:04.912
How could I forget?

02:05.080 --> 02:07.469
- Nice to see you again.
- Nice to see you too.

02:08.520 --> 02:11.637
Courtney and your brother are helping
me with the wedding arrangements.

02:11.800 --> 02:15.839
It's your fifth wedding, Mom.
What do you need help with?

02:16.440 --> 02:18.670
Besides remembering the groom's name?

02:19.720 --> 02:23.793
I'd cut him out of the will if I thought
there was a chance he'd outlive me.

02:25.920 --> 02:28.593
Hello? Oh, Teddy, darling.

02:28.760 --> 02:30.352
What's up?

02:31.040 --> 02:32.268
Excuse me.

02:32.440 --> 02:35.398
That's wonderful.
Can you keep it up till I get there?

02:37.520 --> 02:40.273
All right, I want to make sure
we're all on the same page here.

02:40.440 --> 02:42.510
This wedding will be ruined
if Mom finds out...

02:42.680 --> 02:45.877
...her son and future stepdaughter
have been carrying on behind her back.

02:46.040 --> 02:47.234
- Don't worry.
- She won't.

02:47.400 --> 02:50.551
No, I do worry.
There can be no flirting, no innuendo.

02:51.880 --> 02:55.270
Don't worry about "innuendo,"
worry about "in-her-end-o."

02:57.640 --> 03:00.279
Everybody keeps their troublemakers
in their pants.

03:00.440 --> 03:03.159
Hey, I'll cooperate,
but I can't speak for my troublemaker.

03:04.040 --> 03:07.828
Alan, Teddy wants to talk to you
about the boutonnieres.

03:08.000 --> 03:09.797
Coming.

03:09.960 --> 03:11.996
I knew he'd fight me on this.

03:14.520 --> 03:17.080
So when can we get together?

03:17.240 --> 03:19.674
We can't. You and I are done.

03:20.440 --> 03:23.671
Why? Just because of what Alan said?
Nobody listens to Alan.

03:23.840 --> 03:26.638
Hell, half the time,
Alan doesn't listen to Alan.

03:26.800 --> 03:30.031
I finally have a good relationship
with your mother. I'd like to keep it.

03:30.200 --> 03:33.397
Hey, a good relationship with my mother
is highly overrated.

03:33.560 --> 03:36.279
Look at me,
I've gone my whole life without one.

03:36.440 --> 03:40.592
Charlie, get it through your head.
You and I, no more.

03:43.560 --> 03:47.792
If it were that simple,
they wouldn't call it "troublemaker."

03:57.000 --> 04:00.310
I'd like to make a little toast.
To our families coming together.

04:00.480 --> 04:01.629
Hear, hear.

04:01.800 --> 04:04.155
- To coming together.
- &lt;i>No.&lt;/i>

04:05.440 --> 04:08.671
Evelyn is gaining a daughter
and I'm gaining two sons.

04:08.840 --> 04:11.400
- And a grandson.
- Don't interrupt.

04:11.800 --> 04:15.588
I'd like to say something else. I want
this to be an old-fashioned marriage.

04:15.760 --> 04:18.832
Darling, what's mine is yours.

04:19.000 --> 04:20.353
We do not need a prenup.

04:21.640 --> 04:23.790
Teddy, we've talked about this.

04:23.960 --> 04:26.758
You have a lot of money.
You should be protected.

04:26.920 --> 04:28.876
I don't need to be protected
from you, baby.

04:29.040 --> 04:31.349
- Daddy, wait a minute.
- This is none of your business.

04:31.520 --> 04:33.795
- But, Dad.
- But nothing.

04:33.960 --> 04:35.473
I love this woman.

04:35.640 --> 04:37.551
And I'm not gonna bet
against our marriage...

04:37.720 --> 04:39.517
...by bringing a bunch of lawyers
into it.

04:43.120 --> 04:45.190
- He must really love her.
- Yeah.

04:45.360 --> 04:46.759
The schmuck.

04:48.840 --> 04:50.512
Excuse me.

04:57.400 --> 04:59.960
I had a thought about the ice sculpture.

05:02.080 --> 05:03.559
A lot of people go with Cupid...

05:03.720 --> 05:06.314
...but you gotta remember,
the bow and arrow melts first...

05:06.480 --> 05:09.313
...and what you're left with
is a fat kid dancing in shrimp.

05:11.240 --> 05:12.468
There's gonna be shrimp?

05:13.160 --> 05:14.513
For the guests.

05:14.680 --> 05:18.070
- So what am I?
- Don't feed me straight lines, dear.

05:18.480 --> 05:20.038
Excuse me.

05:21.880 --> 05:24.872
Why would I feed her straight lines
if there's shrimp?

05:37.840 --> 05:41.833
- I'll be out in a minute.
- I can't wait. You'd better let me in now.

05:42.000 --> 05:43.752
Charlie, get out of here.

05:43.920 --> 05:46.593
Oh, come on.
You can't just cut me off like this.

05:46.760 --> 05:50.753
Hey, I can cut off whoever
or whatever I want.

05:51.240 --> 05:53.913
Are you playing hard-to-get
because you know it turns me on?

05:55.080 --> 05:56.752
I'm not playing, Charlie.

05:56.920 --> 06:00.151
Okay, I just have to say,
not playing turns me on more.

06:02.760 --> 06:04.876
Charlie, are you in there
with Courtney?

06:05.040 --> 06:06.598
No.

06:07.560 --> 06:09.437
- Hi, Courtney.
- Hey, Alan.

06:09.840 --> 06:11.512
- I thought we had an agreement.
- Yeah.

06:11.680 --> 06:14.399
The agreement was
Mom doesn't find out.

06:15.400 --> 06:18.119
Courtney? Are you okay, dear?

06:18.280 --> 06:20.350
Oh, I'm fine, Evelyn.

06:20.720 --> 06:24.030
I thought you might be upset
about that prenup nonsense.

06:24.200 --> 06:27.272
And I just want you to know,
I'm not after your father's money.

06:27.440 --> 06:29.351
I'm sure you're not.

06:32.040 --> 06:34.076
Believe me,
I've got plenty of my own money.

06:34.240 --> 06:37.994
Of course, don't tell Alan and Charlie,
they're annoying enough as it is.

06:38.920 --> 06:40.478
I won't.

06:41.880 --> 06:43.438
So exactly how rich are you?

06:44.920 --> 06:45.955
I do all right.

06:47.880 --> 06:50.917
When you marry my grandma,
what does that make you to me?

06:51.720 --> 06:53.312
Nothing.

06:55.440 --> 06:56.509
Sorry, dear.

06:56.680 --> 06:59.035
Oh, that's all right.
I was talking to the kid.

06:59.560 --> 07:02.472
- Isn't that nice?
- You know, even if we're not related...

07:02.640 --> 07:05.598
...you could still buy me
birthday and Christmas presents.

07:05.960 --> 07:07.871
Thanks for the tip.

07:09.000 --> 07:10.399
I don't believe it.

07:10.560 --> 07:14.235
If Mom's got so much money, how come
we still get books for Christmas?

07:15.560 --> 07:16.754
Let it go, Alan.

07:16.920 --> 07:20.549
Whatever money she has most likely
has got an ancient curse attached to it.

07:24.360 --> 07:26.874
- What are you doing?
- I'm here, I figured what the hell?

07:28.840 --> 07:31.593
- Remember to put the seat back down.
- It's a ladies' room.

07:31.760 --> 07:33.432
Why do they even go up?

07:33.600 --> 07:37.752
I don't know. It's a bigger target for
broads who want to puke their dinner.

07:38.640 --> 07:40.039
Makes sense.

07:40.200 --> 07:43.715
All right, let's talk about Courtney.

07:45.280 --> 07:48.590
- What do you want me to tell you?
- Why you're so obsessed with her.

07:48.760 --> 07:51.718
Isn't it obvious?
She drinks, she smokes, she gambles.

07:51.880 --> 07:53.472
She's me with indoor plumbing.

07:58.480 --> 08:00.232
What are you doing in the ladies' room?

08:01.560 --> 08:02.879
The men's room was occupied.

08:03.440 --> 08:04.953
Do you have to pee sitting down?

08:05.360 --> 08:08.193
- No, the seats go up.
- Cool.

08:10.200 --> 08:12.668
Hey, it smells nice in here.

08:19.760 --> 08:22.638
Hey, Courtney.
It's Charlie, your brother.

08:23.920 --> 08:27.913
Anyway, I just wanted to apologize for
making a scene there in the restaurant.

08:28.080 --> 08:30.275
I'd still love to get together,
so give me a call.

08:30.440 --> 08:33.796
I'm just sitting at home,
reading a book.

08:35.760 --> 08:38.274
And watching TV.

08:40.520 --> 08:43.956
Disney Channel, &lt;i>101 Dalmatians.&lt;/i>

08:44.120 --> 08:46.156
What a great film, huh?

08:48.720 --> 08:50.358
Sat on the remote.

08:50.520 --> 08:52.556
Hey, &lt;i>Apocalypse Now.&lt;/i>

08:53.160 --> 08:55.116
Another great movie, huh?

08:55.680 --> 08:58.194
Anyway, call me.

09:04.640 --> 09:07.393
- Hi, Charlie.
- Rose?

09:07.560 --> 09:09.915
What the hell are you doing here?

09:10.080 --> 09:11.718
I could ask you that question.

09:12.440 --> 09:15.273
And the answer would be the same:
Stalking.

09:17.080 --> 09:19.992
- No. No, I'm not...
- Good at it?

09:22.560 --> 09:25.358
- What do you want?
- Right now or long-term?

09:25.520 --> 09:26.589
Rose.

09:26.760 --> 09:31.788
I've just been watching you for an hour
and 38 minutes, and I felt bad for you.

09:31.960 --> 09:33.951
I thought maybe
you could use some help.

09:34.120 --> 09:35.189
Thanks, but I'm fine.

09:35.360 --> 09:37.669
Really? Did you bring water?

09:37.840 --> 09:39.319
No.

09:41.000 --> 09:42.592
Trail mix?

09:42.760 --> 09:44.159
No.

09:46.560 --> 09:48.278
Pee jar?

09:48.560 --> 09:52.075
- That would have been a great idea.
- Here you go.

09:53.480 --> 09:57.632
- Thank you.
- Let's see. What else?

09:57.800 --> 09:59.392
Night-vision goggles?

10:00.520 --> 10:02.431
- I don't think so.
- You say that now...

10:02.600 --> 10:05.751
...but if you hide in her trunk
and wanna do a little light reading...

10:05.920 --> 10:07.035
...you're gonna be sorry.

10:07.200 --> 10:09.794
- I'm fine.
- Okay.

10:09.960 --> 10:12.474
I'll just keep you company.
Give me one of these...

10:12.640 --> 10:14.312
...if you need to use the pee jar.

10:15.560 --> 10:17.357
Charlie, what the hell are you doing?

10:18.520 --> 10:21.637
Hey. Teddy. How are you?

10:21.800 --> 10:23.518
Since when do you drive a Volvo?

10:24.040 --> 10:25.155
It's my brother's car.

10:25.320 --> 10:27.675
Very smart.
She would have spotted your car.

10:27.840 --> 10:29.432
I didn't give you points for that.

10:30.120 --> 10:31.997
I thought you and I
had an understanding...

10:32.160 --> 10:34.879
...you and my daughter weren't
gonna see each other anymore.

10:35.040 --> 10:38.271
In my defense, we're not really
seeing each other. This is more of a...

10:38.440 --> 10:40.476
Reconnaissance mission.

10:40.880 --> 10:42.552
Who is this?

10:44.000 --> 10:45.797
This is Rose, she's kind of my...

10:45.960 --> 10:47.757
Sidekick.

10:48.960 --> 10:51.793
I don't wanna beat this to death,
but if your mother finds out...

10:51.960 --> 10:54.838
...you and Courtney are seeing
each other, and I kept it from her...

10:55.000 --> 10:57.639
...I don't know what she'd do.
Probably call off the wedding.

10:57.800 --> 10:59.950
I'm sorry, Teddy.
I don't want to screw things up.

11:00.120 --> 11:02.395
- Well, then, go home.
- Right.

11:02.920 --> 11:04.478
Nice to meet you, Rose.

11:10.120 --> 11:12.793
Boy, if he was 30 years younger,
I'd be following him.

11:15.080 --> 11:16.911
Oh, what the hell.

11:28.320 --> 11:30.880
You were with her, weren't you?

11:31.440 --> 11:33.351
What are you, my wife?

11:34.960 --> 11:37.758
No, I'm the wedding planner.

11:39.920 --> 11:43.515
I'm the one who's dealing with caterers
and florists and musicians...

11:43.680 --> 11:46.638
...and parking valets
and a thousand frozen butterflies.

11:47.280 --> 11:49.350
- Frozen butterflies?
- Mom wanted butterflies.

11:49.520 --> 11:50.873
What'll she do, eat them?

11:51.040 --> 11:52.951
No, you thaw them out
during the ceremony...

11:53.120 --> 11:55.429
...and when the bride and groom kiss,
they fly away.

11:55.600 --> 11:58.353
- Is there still gonna be shrimp?
- Yes, there's gonna be shrimp.

11:58.520 --> 12:00.158
Good. I like shrimp.

12:02.640 --> 12:04.676
Charlie, I will not have you
ruin this wedding.

12:04.840 --> 12:08.037
Well, you can relax.
I wasn't with Courtney.

12:08.200 --> 12:10.395
Thank God for that.
So where were you?

12:11.760 --> 12:14.115
Parked outside her apartment.

12:15.640 --> 12:16.868
You were stalking her?

12:17.680 --> 12:21.389
Oh, man,
why does everybody use that word?

12:22.320 --> 12:25.756
- It has such a bad connotation.
- Charlie, what is wrong with you?

12:25.920 --> 12:29.754
- I've never seen you like this before.
- I know, I know.

12:30.320 --> 12:32.231
I can't get her out of my mind.

12:32.400 --> 12:35.153
I go to sleep thinking about her,
I wake up thinking about her.

12:35.320 --> 12:37.356
The other day,
I stumbled into a three-way...

12:41.560 --> 12:45.838
- How do you stumble into a three-way?
- It's usually a roommate thing.

12:46.640 --> 12:49.996
You read about sisters,
but that almost never happens.

12:50.520 --> 12:52.192
Anyway, in order to get through it...

12:52.360 --> 12:55.397
...I had to fantasize
that both of them were Courtney.

12:55.560 --> 12:58.438
- How sad is that?
- I'm brokenhearted for you.

13:00.920 --> 13:02.035
You know what I think?

13:02.200 --> 13:05.909
I think the only reason you're obsessed
with Courtney is you can't have her.

13:06.080 --> 13:07.911
Well, duh.

13:08.400 --> 13:12.837
- Oh, please tell me you're not calling her.
- Of course not.

13:15.680 --> 13:18.592
Hey, Rose, it's Charlie.
Listen, after you're done with Teddy...

13:18.760 --> 13:21.558
...can you swing by Courtney's
and let me know what she's doing?

13:28.400 --> 13:31.949
Okay, the vows. Now, I understand
you've written your own?

13:32.120 --> 13:33.394
First I'm hearing about it.

13:33.560 --> 13:37.838
Oh, forgive me, darling.
I took the liberty of writing both of ours.

13:39.920 --> 13:42.639
I come across kind of fruity, don't I?

13:43.240 --> 13:47.472
Well, you're in love with me.
Love makes everyone a little gay.

13:48.520 --> 13:49.714
Terrific.

13:50.720 --> 13:54.030
Please let that be my butterflies.
Please, please, please.

13:55.040 --> 13:57.679
That kid doesn't need butterflies.

13:59.440 --> 14:00.555
Hi, Courtney. Come on in.

14:00.720 --> 14:03.359
No, that's okay.
I just need to talk to my father.

14:03.520 --> 14:06.751
- What's up, baby?
- Is Courtney here?

14:09.200 --> 14:10.519
Hi, Courtney.

14:11.080 --> 14:14.356
Hi, Charlie. Dad, it's kind of private.
Can I talk to you outside, please?

14:14.520 --> 14:15.919
Sure. Excuse me.

14:16.640 --> 14:19.712
Did you happen to see
a frozen-butterfly truck go by?

14:21.200 --> 14:23.919
- Everything okay?
- No, no, everything is not okay.

14:24.080 --> 14:25.399
Always good to see you.

14:26.680 --> 14:30.070
- I don't understand why you won't help.
- Damn it, we've been through this.

14:30.240 --> 14:32.390
- I'm not gonna keep bailing you out.
- But, Daddy...

14:32.560 --> 14:33.788
Don't "But, Daddy" me.

14:33.960 --> 14:37.999
Sure makes you feel grateful
that the three of us get along so well.

14:38.480 --> 14:41.472
- Am I supposed to live on the street?
- Live within your means.

14:41.640 --> 14:43.915
You're just gonna turn your back?
Your own daughter?

14:44.080 --> 14:46.833
- Oh, don't be such a drama queen.
- Forget it, I'm out of here.

14:47.000 --> 14:48.877
Courtney, don't be like that.

14:53.480 --> 14:54.549
Okay, the butterflies.

14:55.600 --> 14:58.637
Now, Mom, when you kiss Teddy,
they're gonna be released on the deck.

14:58.800 --> 15:02.793
But there's a fifty-fifty chance that gulls
will swoop down and rip them to shreds.

15:08.080 --> 15:09.559
I'm sorry you heard that.

15:09.720 --> 15:13.156
- Do you want me to talk to her?
- No, no, leave it alone.

15:13.840 --> 15:15.558
I'll go talk to her.

15:18.960 --> 15:22.839
Would either of you care to explain
why he's going to talk to her?

15:23.800 --> 15:25.677
- No.
- No.

15:30.160 --> 15:32.390
- Hi.
- What are you doing here?

15:33.040 --> 15:36.396
I was concerned about you.
I thought maybe I could help.

15:36.840 --> 15:38.637
You can't help me.

15:39.480 --> 15:41.118
Try me.

15:43.680 --> 15:45.193
I was looking at the wrong window.

15:48.320 --> 15:51.357
- What?
- Nice place.

15:54.280 --> 15:56.748
So, what's going on?

15:57.480 --> 15:59.436
What do you want me to tell you,
Charlie?

15:59.600 --> 16:02.273
I lost my job,
I'm about to lose my condo...

16:02.440 --> 16:05.352
...and my father won't lift a finger
to help me.

16:07.360 --> 16:09.032
How much do you need?

16:09.200 --> 16:11.031
Forget it, I can't take your money.

16:12.480 --> 16:14.471
Well, I hadn't actually offered yet.

16:16.400 --> 16:20.712
But we are gonna be family,
and family looks after each other.

16:20.880 --> 16:22.359
I need $50,000.

16:26.840 --> 16:28.558
How about if I talk to your dad?

16:29.920 --> 16:31.512
It's no use.

16:31.680 --> 16:33.955
He's trying to teach me a lesson.

16:35.800 --> 16:38.553
You know, I just
love this place so much.

16:40.120 --> 16:41.997
I put every dime I had into it.

16:45.120 --> 16:46.792
Charlie, what am I gonna do?

16:48.720 --> 16:51.234
You're gonna take
the money from me.

16:52.080 --> 16:53.433
No.

16:53.600 --> 16:55.158
No, it wouldn't be right.

16:55.320 --> 16:57.276
I insist.

17:00.080 --> 17:01.991
&lt;i>Really?&lt;/i>

17:03.600 --> 17:04.874
I promise I'll pay you back.

17:05.520 --> 17:06.873
I know you will.

17:07.600 --> 17:09.318
Thank you.

17:09.480 --> 17:11.198
So much.

17:19.160 --> 17:22.197
No, no, no, that's not why
I'm doing this.

17:22.360 --> 17:24.555
I know, I know, but I want you.

17:27.800 --> 17:28.915
I want you too...

17:29.080 --> 17:33.039
...but I don't wanna feel like we're
doing this because I lent you money.

17:33.200 --> 17:36.954
Okay, okay. But soon?

17:37.880 --> 17:39.279
Definitely soon.

17:47.720 --> 17:49.836
- Good night.
- Night.

17:53.840 --> 17:56.991
Oh, hell, if you're okay with it,
I'm okay with it.

18:02.960 --> 18:05.918
"And I promise to honor
and cherish you...

18:06.080 --> 18:09.117
...to always be there for you
as a trusted friend...

18:09.280 --> 18:12.750
...devoted husband and selfish lover."

18:13.640 --> 18:14.789
"Selfless."

18:15.480 --> 18:17.038
Oh, right, selfless.

18:19.280 --> 18:22.033
"And even though
I'm significantly older than you...

18:24.160 --> 18:26.549
...I feel renewed and replenished...

18:26.720 --> 18:30.349
...every time I drink
the sweet nectar of your youth."

18:31.080 --> 18:34.277
Pick it up, Teddy.
No one can see butterflies in the dark.

18:36.280 --> 18:38.999
"I remember the first time
I laid eyes on you...

18:39.480 --> 18:45.077
...at one of the many charity events to
which you so tirelessly devote yourself.

18:45.600 --> 18:49.878
You were a vision in Dolce &amp; Gabbana
and compassion.

18:50.880 --> 18:55.510
And that first moment we spoke,
the simple melody of your voice...

18:55.680 --> 18:59.116
...was testimony
to how much the world lost...

18:59.280 --> 19:03.193
...when you gave up
a very promising singing career...

19:04.000 --> 19:06.195
...in order to raise your two little boys.

19:06.720 --> 19:09.439
Not that they ever appreciated it.

19:11.520 --> 19:13.590
And the lovemaking...

19:13.760 --> 19:16.433
...what can I say
about the lovemaking?"

19:17.840 --> 19:21.515
- I can't say this.
- Lf you don't, I will.

19:26.080 --> 19:31.359
"As I explored every inch of your firm,
non-surgically-enhanced body...

19:32.800 --> 19:37.078
...I finally learned the meaning
of the words 'heaven on earth'...

19:38.400 --> 19:40.072
...and 'natural redhead.'

19:46.400 --> 19:47.958
In the words of the Bard:

19:48.360 --> 19:51.989
&lt;i>Shall I compare thee&lt;/i>
&lt;i>to the summer's day?&lt;/i>

19:52.160 --> 19:54.958
&lt;i>Thou art more lovely&lt;/i>
&lt;i>and more temperate.&lt;/i>

19:55.120 --> 19:59.352
&lt;i>Rough winds do shake&lt;/i>
&lt;i>The darling buds of May&lt;/i>

19:59.520 --> 20:00.919
&lt;i>Will you marry me?&lt;/i>

20:01.080 --> 20:03.310
&lt;i>And summer's lease&lt;/i>
&lt;i>hath all to short a date.&lt;/i>

20:03.480 --> 20:04.469
- &lt;i>Really?&lt;/i>
- &lt;i>Yes.&lt;/i>

20:04.640 --> 20:06.710
- &lt;i>So long as men can breathe&lt;/i>
- &lt;i>Yes.&lt;/i>

20:06.880 --> 20:08.632
- &lt;i>Our eyes can see&lt;/i>
- &lt;i>Really?&lt;/i>

20:08.800 --> 20:13.430
&lt;i>So long lives this,&lt;/i>
&lt;i>and gives life to thee. "

20:14.240 --> 20:16.629
You may now kiss the bride.

20:28.560 --> 20:32.075
Do you want me to sweep them up
and pop them in the microwave?

20:34.960 --> 20:36.678
&lt;i>Never mind.&lt;/i>

21:00.680 --> 21:02.671
